            "target_entity_instance": "model",
            "target_entity_type": "SourceType",
            "paragraph": "To estimate the uncertainties associated with the generation of storm composites from coarse-resolution, non-tide-corrected shoreline data, we performed a comparative validation using a high-resolution (275 m-spaced), tide-corrected shoreline dataset (HRTC) developed by Graffin et al.31. This dataset spans the western coast of North America and was produced using the Shoreliner extraction toolkit59. Tidal corrections were applied using the FES2022 global tide model67, and the product has been bench-marked against high-frequency in situ measurements at Torrey Pines, yielding performance metrics consistent with state-of-the-art methods5.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
